) ([Amazon](https://www.amazon.com/gp/video/detail/B0CPQ7GRYC/ref=atv_dp_share_cu_r), [Apple TV](https://tv.apple.com/us/movie/american-fiction/umc.cmc.5qme2234943x7zjd9iou9eae3)). _American Fiction_ is probably my favorite movie of the last 1–2 years. I’ve become obsessed with it, and you’ll laugh your ass off. I caught it last week at the theaters on a whim, and I’ve already watched it a second time to try and deconstruct the magic. It’s a comedic Trojan Horse of epic proportions. Don’t trust the streaming descriptions; _American Fiction_ is about much more. Every character is flawed in their own beautiful, human way, and the writing hits a home run. Ambiguities are left in so that the movie becomes your own Rorschach test. Huge kudos to everyone involved, including 2024 Oscar nominees [Cord Jefferson](https://twitter.com/cordjefferson) (Best Adapted Screenplay) and [Jeffrey Wright](https://twitter.com/jfreewright) (Best Actor). Thanks to [Orion Pictures](https://twitter.com/OrionPictures) and [MGM Studios](https://twitter.com/mgmstudios) for having the stones to back this marvel. You can now also [watch it at home](https://www.amazon.com/American-Fiction-Jeffrey-Wright/dp/B0CPQ8CSST/). It currently has a 95% audience score on [Rotten Tomatoes](https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/american_fiction), and you can find the trailer [here](https://youtu.be/i0MbLCpYJPA?feature=shared).  
